# Under Camouflage each creature in a pile blocks the attacker the pile went to if it can (CR 509.1b): the blocks the piles
# make must still be a legal set together, and Caverns of Despair's "no more than two creatures can block each combat" is
# a restriction on the whole (CR 509.1b), so of three creatures named to block only two do (CR 509.1c), the defending
# player choosing which. The first pile (the die's face 1) goes to the first Memnite: the first two Ornithopters are in
# it, the third Ornithopter in the second pile. Bot2 may not block with all three, nor with fewer than two, nor make a
# block no pile named.
[Bot1 Deck]
Caverns of Despair
Black Lotus
Mox Ruby
Memnite x2
Forest
Camouflage
Mountain x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter x3
Island x20

[Dice]
1

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Caverns of Despair.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Memnite#1 > Bot2; Memnite#2 > Bot2)
Bot1.Hand.Camouflage.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Choose(Ornithopter#1; Ornithopter#2)
Bot2.Choose(Ornithopter#3)
! Bot2.Block(Ornithopter#1 > Memnite#1; Ornithopter#2 > Memnite#1; Ornithopter#3 > Memnite#2)
! Bot2.Block(Ornithopter#1 > Memnite#1)
! Bot2.Block(Ornithopter#1 > Memnite#2)
! Bot2.Block(Count: 0)
Bot2.Block(Ornithopter#1 > Memnite#1; Ornithopter#3 > Memnite#2)
? Combat.Blocks = Ornithopter > Memnite; Ornithopter > Memnite
? Combat.Blockers.Count = 2
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 20
Bot1.Battlefield.Caverns of Despair.Types = Enchantment
